CORE
main.c

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ not recorded: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
malloc recorded its object in __CPROVER_new_object for the delete[] checks
in C programs too, which cost 5 to 43 symex steps per aws-c-common proof.
cbmc-cpp/cpp98_array_delete_after_malloc checks that C++ programs still
record it.
